      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raja lived alone in the forest and grew tired of eating raw meat every day. One evening, he smelled something wonderful drifting from a village and followed it to a wedding feast. He watched from the trees as the cook layered rice, spices and meat in a huge pot, and decided he had to learn this magic.\n\nThe next morning, Raja crept to the cook's house and left a basket of mangoes at the door. The cook, touched by the gift, began leaving him small portions of biryani each week. Raja studied every layer, every spice, practising in secret with a clay pot he found by the river.\n\nMonths later, Raja invited all the forest animals to a feast. They arrived nervously, but when he lifted the lid, the fragrance made everyone forget their fear. The biryani was perfect—tender, fragrant, just the right heat. From that day, Raja became the forest's beloved cook, and no one went hungry again.\n\n6:38 PM",
